  "methodology": "Fresh temporary locked Cargo project and separate release target per source. Source and fixture creation/build occur outside timings. Each process opens Corpus once, runs the working API then committed API, and returns all sample distributions. API timings include record loading, parsing, schema/corpus validation, hashing and materialization; post-call assertions are excluded. Both invocations inherit the same host Git-read environment; fixture creation excludes host/system Git configuration. Baseline production sources are 1ca7a26 with a regression-test-only overlay that is not compiled in release. Candidate is the recorded copied working source fingerprint, whose Store reader was committed as 899b99d. The reproducible harness now strips ambient GIT_* before fixture, metadata, build and benchmark subprocesses, setting explicit private identities/config/date fields; a hostile-override check preserves a foreign temporary repository unchanged.",
  "interpretation": "Synthetic maximum-size question-kind corpus on one macOS host, not a universal throughput guarantee. Reopening Git for every record is avoided; a repository and pinned tree live only for one committed snapshot. Working API medians vary under host load; all three committed medians improved substantially.",
